## G0-G5 execution order

### G0 - exact bytes and rights

First receipt and quarantine the exact post-V13 30 mL package without selecting a canonical formula. Recover only unchanged originals for the five unavailable package hashes if they become available. Bind field-specific reuse rights, then run strict receipt, quarantine, graph, and field mapping. Never reconstruct or substitute missing parents.

### G1 - native stock and preparation closure

Close CLR-001 2-Acetyl Pyrazine and CLR-002 Lemonile with exact stock, carrier, lot, parent-stock, measured quantity, and preparation receipts. Preserve every other readiness hold.

### G2 - real package bench prerequisites

The software metadata contract is complete. The next input is physical evidence: four actual preparations, nine verifications, and nine authenticated references. Record planned, measured, committed, corrected, and reversed grains distinctly.

Observed pre-mix v/v may be calculated only from separately measured component delivery volumes with compatible conditions and uncertainty. A final mixed-solution volume is invalid. Any missing or mismatched method, device, calibration, operator, time, temperature, condition, or uncertainty keeps alignment on HOLD.

### G3 - protocol lock and physical authorization

Bind one selected source candidate through C10 and P3 using exact formula, fork, stock, matrix, and qualification hashes. Then separately authorize the native Laboratory Beta chain:

`LabExperiment -> bottle-bound LabSample -> LabApplication -> LabObservation`

No bottle means no sample or execution.

### G4 - first native experiment

After stock and preparation closure, run the governed concentration-aware binary-mixture benchmark. Compare the linear-quality and strongest-component-intensity baselines before fitting any nonlinear residual interaction model.

### G5 - sensory and release

Bind all 17 C0 artifacts, assessor qualifications, expected cells, and human-execution authorization. Revalidate semantic readback after persistence. Only then run quick and full project verification for a release decision.

